WEBVTT

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:11.320
Cheerful, pounding heart. Cheerful, pounding heart.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:15.700
Cheerful, pounding heart. Cheerful, pounding heart.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.700
Cheerful!

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:18.870
Pounding!

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.290
Heart!

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:41.770
All the laughter, all the tears—everything happened just to meet you

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.430
Always go

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.850
On my own

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.070
Always go

00:00:54.950 --> 00:01:00.740
The wind blows my overflowing tears away (the wind blows them away)

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:08.130
I try to reach out my hand time after time toward what's to come

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:14.170
I've been hurt before by careless words

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:23.140
It's time I move forward with that unchangeable past

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.640
All the laughter, all the tears—

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:36.280
everything that has happened brought me to you

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:42.330
All we have left is the future

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:48.750
Please become our reason to continue living

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:55.470
And then the sun will once again shine on us

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:10.440
I didn't know there was a place like this in Shinjuku...

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.480
If a Machine Goodfellow activated in the middle of a city like this,

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.110
it could get ugly.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.950
The Machine Goodfellows are mind-machine interfaces tuned specifically

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:25.330
to each Designer's Child for optimal use of their mobile weapons.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:30.420
Designer's Children are able to use these personalized
machines to manipulate advanced weaponry

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.960
as though it were an extension of their own bodies.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.800
But there's something even more interesting.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:42.140
Yomatsuri Akari acquired the primary manual for this,

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.310
the Machine Goodfellow's background operations system.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.520
According to the manual,

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:54.400
by loading a capsule filled with Orgone energy into its head,

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.610
the consciousness of the Designer's Child inside

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.410
can be transferred into a Kill-T-Gang.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.950
The Kill-T-Gangs require Orgone energy in order to function.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.330
Orgone energy...

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:11.250
The energy released when the Livlaster fires is one form it can come in.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:15.290
The reason they tried to force Hana to manifest the Livlaster

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.050
was to use its energy.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.760
We've also learned

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:26.100
that once an Orgone energy capsule has been loaded into a Machine Goodfellow,

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.850
the energy transfer to the Kill-T-Gang takes precisely three minutes and fifty-nine seconds.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:31.190
Meaning?

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:36.320
If you can remove its head before those three minutes and fifty-nine seconds have elapsed,

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.440
the Kill-T-Gang won't be able to activate.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.780
Three minutes and fifty-nine seconds...

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:44.570
So the head is the weak point...

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:48.540
This is really impressive, Science Chief.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.080
Not at all.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:55.880
Frankly, this was only possible because Akari managed to infiltrate the enemy's systems

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.210
during the last battle and retrieve all this data.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:05.010
You're such a gentleman, saying "retrieve" instead of "steal."

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.050
So she's their weak point?

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:12.140
She's the pest who hacked the Machine Goodfellow?

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:15.350
She doesn't look like much of a fighter.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.900
That's our target.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.440
She's still a child, even.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:26.780
Magical Girl Akari

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:26.770
Magical Girl Akari

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:44.840
Ai's

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:39.550
Ice Cream Love

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:45.830
Ice Cream Love

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:45.840
Ai's New Single
Ice Cream Love

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.770
It's even bigger than it looked online!

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.440
So good...

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.360
It really is good.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.410
It feels like we're always eating.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.200
Pitz, you have some, too.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:15.410
Another Machine Goodfellow is going to activate tonight, right?

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:16.870
Yes.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:21.500
But Pitz says he doesn't know any more than that.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.670
That much alone is amazing.

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:29.260
If one does activate, we can use the MM bus to locate it.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:34.560
Defeating it in three minutes and fifty-nine seconds will be the main problem.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.480
It'll be close.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.520
There are two kinds of close.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.940
A close win and a close loss.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:49.660
Well, just leave it to the magical girl!

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:59.630
It would be ideal if we could locate their Machine Goodfellow ahead of time.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:04.050
But all the same, this area is really populated.

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:06.090
It makes me uneasy.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:10.340
A fight in the middle of a city like this would definitely be bad...

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.310
I doubt our enemy wants to attract the attention, either.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:16.520
Finding them could prove difficult.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:20.610
Okay, then...

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.400
Where are you going?

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.150
A magic item...

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.450
I'm going to buy a computer.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.450
I broke mine during the last mission.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.950
Then I'll go with you.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.540
I'll be fine.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.660
I know Shinjuku like the back of my hand.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:40.370
And finding the Machine Goodfellow is more important.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.000
But...

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.380
I'll be fine...

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.710
I can protect myself.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:51.550
So I'll be going AWOL to enjoy myself for a while.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.930
You take care of the rest, Captain.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:59.560
Seriously, do you <i>have</i> to keep calling me that?

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:04.900
I'm the only one not contributing to the team...

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:11.490
Nippon   Seinenkan   Hall

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.490
Nippon Seinenkan Hall

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:11.530
Ai

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.450
Ai Summer

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.450
You don't want to sing?

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:18.200
I'm afraid to sing.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:19.790
Let's see...

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:27.510
You're referring to tonight's concert,

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.420
not your long-term career as an idol, right?

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.260
Listen, Ai...

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.310
Cheerful!

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:37.390
Pounding!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.600
Heart!

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.770
Isn't that your catchphrase?

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:46.610
Everyone loses confidence in themselves sometimes!

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.610
I've never had any self-confidence.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.030
What are you saying?

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.610
We've both worked so hard to reach this point!

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.200
A Popular Idol's

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.200
Lonely Past

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.200
Her

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.200
cheerfulness

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.200
is fake ?!

00:07:56.450 --> 00:08:00.790
You saw that magazine?

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:59.200
A Popular Idol's Lonely Past

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:05.750
Ignore what the tabloids say!

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:08.840
So you grew up in an orphanage and never went to school.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.880
Her cheerfulness is fake?!

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:11.010
What's wrong with that?

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:14.010
Idols are supposed to be special...

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:17.470
In fact, having something that makes you different is a great weapon.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.310
That doesn't matter.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:24.600
What if everyone hates me?

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.570
Would I be all alone again?

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:35.570
If they really didn't like you, no one would come to your concerts.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:38.240
Tonight's another full house, isn't it?

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:43.460
Maybe I'm just not cut out to be an idol...

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.750
You're going to be fine!

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:49.340
New girls enter the industry all the time.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.630
Miss, are you interested in being an idol?

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:57.340
I'm a scout for a talent agency...

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:01.060
Oh, you're interested in me?

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:02.850
You have a good eye...

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:05.600
Hello.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.560
The dealer...

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:38.970
Hey, there...

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:49.480
Whoa, are you okay, honey?

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:50.360
Wow.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:52.900
You must really love her, man...

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.530
Here's your magic item.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:01.450
Yeah, we've used every trick in the book just getting this far,

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.990
but it's really going to come down to how well her next album sells.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.870
She's lost confidence in herself.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.750
It'll be tough to keep going now.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:13.590
Honestly, I think she has the talent...

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.920
Hello, Ai!

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:26.270
Your manager was just telling her boss that they're nearly through with you.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.890
Are you with the theater staff?

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:32.190
Do I look like I'm with the theater staff?

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.730
Who are you?

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:37.900
If you came in without permission, security will get involved.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.820
I guess you could say...

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:44.370
I'm a scout.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.070
It's been a while, Malkin.

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:18.780
How does it feel to be awake, Aiatar?

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:25.370
I'll take away your happiness like a vampire.

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:31.970
Eyecatch

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:36.090
Welcome back.

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:39.050
Hey, I can't reach Akari...

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:40.420
What's going on?

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.470
She said she was going to buy a computer.

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:47.470
And you let her go off on her own, Captain?

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:49.980
You're calling me that, too?

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.350
Do you normally turn off your phone when you're shopping?

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:55.400
She's probably just off screwing around.

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:13.420
Morning, script kiddie.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:17.090
You're wrong. She's a magical girl.

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:20.300
A magical girl?

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:25.510
That's what she calls herself, so that's what she must be.

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:27.600
That's amazing!

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:29.430
A magical girl, huh?

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.020
Akari hasn't returned yet.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:43.030
And the time Hana predicted is approaching.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:46.660
Without Akari, this operation's odds of success are significantly diminished.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.450
Where's she gone off to?

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.370
She needs to understand her position.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.210
Akari isn't like that.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:58.790
When there's a job for her, she always does it.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.760
You're right.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.340
I'll be standing by in the Ordinary.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.520
You're right... I'm sorry.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:15.270
Has something happened to Akari?

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:23.240
I really hate all those Globe Impactors.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:25.950
Hey, magical girl.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:32.450
Couldn't you use your magic powers to put them all out of commission?

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:38.580
We know you've got the technical skills for it.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.970
Do it now, magical girl.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:52.930
Fine.

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:03.530
A concert without an audience, huh?

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:09.320
It seems kind of pathetic, but I guess I'll do it.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.540
Abreaction!

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:28.800
MM bus signal detected.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:30.050
This is...

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.850
Shinjuku Development Zone 2!

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:39.600
Begin the launch.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.560
You won't make it that far.

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:44.820
And that's probably an artillery type.

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:47.190
If it sees you, it'll shoot you down.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.990
That's a lot better than fighting in the middle of town.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.700
Just do it, please!

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:54.330
Vice Commander!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.620
Roger that, Captain.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:56.540
Teppei?

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.210
Initiating launch sequence.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.210
Wait...

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:39.330
Here goes, Captain.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:40.540
Do it!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.710
Earth Engine Ordinary, launch!

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:51.380
It isn't going to make it.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:53.970
It's okay.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:55.890
The captain will make it.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:59.470
I'm counting on you, Livlaster!

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.000
You're a wimp.

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:31.220
Daichi!

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.050
No more bets.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:38.890
He's hiding behind the building.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:42.060
Either way, if time runs out, we win.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.270
Cheerful artillery... I'm totally invincible.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.360
It isn't coming to finish him off.

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:49.150
They realize they're better off waiting for the transformation to complete?

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:53.820
Will we have to submit a request for the low-orbit Impactors?

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:56.070
What?

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:59.580
The low-orbit Impactors are being hacked.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:02.000
Sixty percent are non-responsive!

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.250
What's happening?

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:05.750
Nice...

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:08.540
Now Globe's Impactors can't activate.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:13.380
In other words, if she can become a Kill-T-Gang, we win.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.550
We're running out of time...

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:21.310
Hiding is pointless...

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:22.180
I'm going!

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.230
They'll shoot you if you go out there!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.400
Even if it's close, I have to do it!

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:32.480
There are only two types of close.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:33.860
You understand, don't you, Captain?

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:36.030
Yeah, I do!

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:49.670
Captain!

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.260
He's out of weapons!

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.720
The end.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.340
I still have one!

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.310
I told you that it's over!

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:08.900
Time's up, Neoteny.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:11.400
Pierce through it, Livlaster!

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:19.110
What?

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.770
That was close, in a lot of ways...

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:51.730
What about Akari?

00:18:57.860 --> 00:18:58.990
He got me.

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:03.200
Whining. Whimpering. Miserable.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:06.080
I wonder if I can still make it to the concert.

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:10.460
I love my fans so much, I could just eat them up.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:12.880
I guess I'll sing for them.

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:20.130
Hi! This is your lovey-dovey little bunny!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.260
Yup.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:23.050
Yup.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.510
Yup...

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.310
I see, okay.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.650
Aiatar screwed up.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:35.440
Oh...

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:44.620
To get even, maybe we'll have her make all the Globe bases self-destruct.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:48.330
You can do it, can't you, magical girl?

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:55.040
More than ninety percent of Globe's low-orbit Impactors are currently unresponsive.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:57.630
Does Akari have something to do with that?

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:02.840
There's a good chance that the enemy is using

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:05.390
her skills and knowledge of Globe's secrets.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:10.560
Globe is trying to trace her location via the route of the breach,

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:14.860
but she's bounced off so many servers that they can't trace her...

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:17.110
It's my fault.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:21.190
I shouldn't have let her go alone.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:31.870
Is it done?

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:34.370
Answer me.

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:36.840
Have you done what I ordered you to?

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:41.050
If I could have avoided it, I'd have preferred not to use this magic.

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:46.220
After all, I can only use it once.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:50.770
A second time, and they'll be
watching for it, so it won't work...

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:52.930
What are you talking about?

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:56.150
All of the nuclear weapons aboard the low-orbit Impactors,

00:20:56.150 --> 00:21:01.070
as well as every single Russian, Chinese, and American ICBM, will all be launched at once.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:05.660
If you don't release me in ten minutes,

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:07.910
Earth will be reduced to a nuclear wasteland.

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:10.660
Are you an idiot?

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:13.210
If you do that, humanity will be wiped out.

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:15.920
Teppei's a good, honest kid.

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:21.300
And he told me about how the Planetary Gears

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:25.340
came to our Solar System and waited for humanity to evolve.

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:29.550
He also told me that waiting so long nearly drove you insane.

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:35.310
If the missiles are launched, all of humanity will be exterminated.

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:38.270
But all that means for us is death.

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:40.980
You won't be able to die,

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:47.410
but how long will you have to wait for another sentient source of Orgone energy

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:51.160
to evolve in this Solar System?

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.580
A few hundred million years?

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.870
A few billion years?

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:07.510
This is bad... She's serious!

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:10.260
She's really going to launch the nukes!

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:10.800
What?

00:22:31.160 --> 00:22:33.540
Hey, I've got one more thing to tell you.

00:22:36.500 --> 00:22:42.000
Don't ever think that an alien could beat a magical girl!

00:22:44.420 --> 00:22:54.970
The gentle breeze sweeps away even tears

00:22:54.970 --> 00:23:00.440
Even the recollections of the way of the stars

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:05.280
aren't always good things

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:12.950
I met you again on that faraway day

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:22.420
Even though we're as close as we are, this distant day is beginning

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:30.680
You can hear my voice calling out when I'm all alone

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:36.640
More than just love, it's hard to put into words

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:42.480
I'm searching for what to say while I walk beside you

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:45.570
Instead of saying goodbye,

00:23:45.570 --> 00:23:53.740
I'll just put these love spun tears in my right pocket again tomorrow

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:57.160
Love is spreading across the world

00:23:57.160 --> 00:24:03.290
And I finally found it, by your side

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:18.310
The Midsummer's Knights rush to repair the damaged Earth Engine,

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:22.480
but the Planetary Gears quickly activate a new Machine Goodfellow.

00:24:22.980 --> 00:24:24.560
In the midst of a fierce battle,

00:24:24.560 --> 00:24:27.190
the Earth Engine finally lets an enemy escape.

00:24:27.610 --> 00:24:28.900
What will Teppei do?

00:24:29.940 --> 00:24:32.280
Next time, on episode 10 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:33.150 --> 00:24:34.610
On the Windy Planet.

00:24:33.220 --> 00:24:35.550
On the Windy Planet

00:24:35.030 --> 00:24:37.280
Earth Engine, scramble!
